{
  "_README": [
    "Hand-written truth: what a person actually sees in each place.",
    "Corrected against the photos by the team - do not regenerate from the model.",
    "",
    "This is NOT produced by the model. It is what we measure the model against:",
    "  object recall      = how many of these the indexer found",
    "  false positives    = things it reported that are not here",
    "  attribute accuracy = did it get the colour right",
    "",
    "Listed PER LOCATION, not per photo, because that is what a query resolves",
    "against after multi-view merging. `views` records which photos show it -",
    "an object visible in only one view is exactly what merging has to rescue.",
    "",
    "`scope` is the honest bookkeeping:",
    "  in   - we intend to index and find this. Counts towards recall.",
    "  out  - deliberately excluded (a fixture, or supplied by the building).",
    "         Reported separately so recall is not quietly inflated.",
    "",
    "`vocab_gap: true` means the object IS indexed but cannot be searched for by",
    "name, because OBJECT_SYNONYMS has no entry. Those are real misses from a",
    "user's point of view and belong in the failure-case section of the report."
  ],
